course: dictionary
lesson: 3707
title: Flee: running from danger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To flee means to run away quickly from danger or from a place. Other words like run or leave are close, but flee is stronger: people flee from fire, floods or war, because they must get away to be safe.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Millions of Ukrainians fled» and «forced from their homes» show that the danger is serious, so flee means more than just going away. Try your meaning in the sentence: "ran away quickly from danger" still fits, so you have it right.
explain: Flee changes its form: flee, flees, fled, fleeing. Fled is the past tense, so «Yanukovych fled to Russia» tells you it already happened. Fleeing shows the action is going on. Spell it fled, not fleed.
explain: A refugee is someone who fled war or danger to their life. A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life. The context tells you the difference: a migrant is not always running from danger.
fact: To flee means to run away from danger or from a place, quickly.
fact: The forms are flee, flees, fled and fleeing.
fact: «Fled in terror» means ran away because of great fear.
fact: A refugee is someone who fled war or danger to their life.
fact: A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life, so a migrant is not always fleeing danger.
fact: In science, animals flee from predators, which means they run away quickly to stay alive.
exercise: The UN reported that more than 12 million people in Sudan were forced from their homes, many fleeing to neighbouring countries. What does fleeing mean here? | Going shopping for food | *Running away quickly from danger to a safer place | Staying at home to rest | Building new houses
exercise: Which word is the past tense of flee? | flies | fleed | flees | *fled
exercise: What is a refugee? | A child who plays in the park | *Someone who fled war or danger to their life | A person who builds houses | Someone who moves abroad to find work
test: «Yanukovych fled to Russia.» What does fled tell you? | He danced at a party | He waited for a bus | *He ran away quickly from danger | He bought a new car
test: «Fled in terror» means | Cried loudly in a playground | Walked slowly to the shops | *Ran away quickly because of great fear | Stood still and calm
exam: A migrant moves to another country, often for work or a better life. Is a migrant always fleeing danger? | Yes, every migrant is fleeing war | Yes, migrants always run from fire | *No, a migrant often moves for work or a better life | No, migrants never move at all
